{"version":"v0.9","updateDataModel":{"surfaceId":"issue-detail","path":"/issue","value":{"key":"EXP-482","project":"Exponential · Web App","title":"Sync stalls when reconnecting after the laptop wakes from sleep","status":"In Progress","priority":"High","assignee":"Alex Acme","reporter":"Mara Lindqvist","createdAt":"2026-10-20T09:14:00Z","description":"After the machine wakes from sleep, the websocket reconnects but **pending mutations are never flushed**. The status indicator stays on *Syncing…* until the tab is reloaded.

**Steps to reproduce**
1. Open any project and edit an issue title
2. Put the laptop to sleep for at least 5 minutes
3. Wake it and make another edit

**Expected:** both edits sync within a few seconds.

**Actual:** the second edit is queued indefinitely; `syncQueue.length` keeps growing.","comments":[{"id":"c1","author":"Jonas Weber","createdAt":"2026-10-20T11:02:00Z","body":"Reproduced on Chrome 131 and Safari 19. Looks like the heartbeat timer isn't restarted after `visibilitychange`."},{"id":"c2","author":"Alex Acme","createdAt":"2026-10-21T15:40:00Z","body":"Confirmed — the reconnect handler resets the socket but not the flush scheduler. I have a fix on a branch, adding a regression test now."},{"id":"c3","author":"Mara Lindqvist","createdAt":"2026-10-23T08:25:00Z","body":"Thanks! Can we also surface a *Reconnecting…* state in the indicator so users know what's happening?"}]}}}
